<%#
  FR-017, design.md §6.9. Served for an unknown or deleted code.

  The stylesheet is inlined, and it is a copy — banned.html.erb (T084) carries
  its own. Two copies of forty lines that never change is cheaper to reason
  about than an asset-pipeline dependency on the anonymous-visitor path, and
  Principle I makes anything added to that path expensive to justify
  (design.md §8, P7).

  No webfont is loaded. Figtree and JetBrains Mono are the app's faces; a
  round trip to fetch one on the path the whole project optimises for buys
  nothing a visitor will notice.

  Themed by `prefers-color-scheme` rather than by the app's `.dark` class,
  because there is no JavaScript here to set the class.
%>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
    <title>This link doesn&rsquo;t exist &middot; Snip</title>
    <style>
      :root {
        color-scheme: light;
        --background: oklch(0.985 0.006 85);
        --foreground: oklch(0.255 0.018 55);
        --muted-foreground: oklch(0.505 0.022 62);
        --primary: oklch(0.555 0.155 42);
        --destructive: oklch(0.545 0.205 27);
        --border: oklch(0.895 0.013 78);
      }

      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root {
          color-scheme: dark;
          --background: oklch(0.175 0.005 58);
          --foreground: oklch(0.87 0.004 85);
          --muted-foreground: oklch(0.735 0.007 75);
          --primary: oklch(0.72 0.145 48);
          --destructive: oklch(0.665 0.185 25);
          --border: oklch(0.32 0.006 58);
        }
      }

      * { box-sizing: border-box; }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--background);
        color: var(--foreground);
        font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
        font-size: 15px;
        line-height: 24px;
      }

      .container { max-width: 480px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 64px 24px; }
      .display { font-size: 32px; line-height: 40px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 16px; }
      .body { margin: 0 0 24px; }
      .body-sm { font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px; color: var(--muted-foreground); margin: 0; }
      .rule { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin: 32px 0; }
      .link { color: var(--primary); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
      .link:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--primary); outline-offset: 2px; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="container">
      <h1 class="display">This link doesn&rsquo;t exist</h1>

      <p class="body">It may have been deleted, or the address may have a typo.</p>

      <hr class="rule">

      <p class="body">
        Snip turns long web addresses into short ones that are easy to share, and
        counts how many people open them.
      </p>

      <p class="body-sm">
        <a class="link" href="<%= "#{Rails.application.config.x.app_url}/signup" %>">Create a free account</a>
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
